  "note": "Both inequalities are valid, but the second is vacuous: |(h−h_H)/t|_∞ = ∞ because h_H(t) decays only like 1/log(1/t) as t → 0+ (see (A.36)). The step needs η◦ = h·η♦ = t³(2−t)³e^{−(t−1)²/2} (the explicit formula of (A.2), also Lean's MajorArcs.etaO), not the printed 'h(t)η♥(t)'."
